// The question: can I afford a 3,000 USD trip in June?
//
// The trip is written as contracts: the flights in March and the hotel and the rest in
// June. The trip fund pays what it holds (`trip-fund -> hotel`, the parcels tied to it),
// and checking pays the rest. A contract's occurrences are only forecast until the journal
// says they happened; take them out and run `axiom forecast` again to see the difference
// (outputs/forecast-without-the-trip.txt).

/// Flights, from the trip fund: about 1,150.00 USD.
contract flights with airline
  1_150 USD yearly on 03-10 from trip-fund
  from 2026-03-10

/// The hotel and the spending money. The trip fund will hold about 2,500.00 USD by
/// then, so it pays what is left of it, and checking pays the rest.
contract hotel-stay with hotel
  1_350 USD yearly on 06-14 from trip-fund
  from 2026-06-14

contract spending-money with hotel
  500 USD yearly on 06-14 from checking
  from 2026-06-14
